In-Reply-To: <AhbRZ42CCQ8.a4gTwD8-AgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <AhbRZ42CCQ8.a4gTwD8-AgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/AhbRZ42CCQ8/m/EwMowN0ABgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

Code example to define adjacency as points within a certain cutoff:

n <- 30
xy <- cbind(runif(n), runif(n))
cutoff <- 0.1
j <- lapply(1:n, function(i)
   setdiff(which(sqrt((xy[,1]-xy[i,1])^2 +
                      (xy[,2]-xy[i,2])^2)<cutoff),i))
nn <- sapply(j,length)
graph <- sparseMatrix(i=rep(1:n, nn), j=unlist(j),
                       x=rep(1, sum(nn)), dims=c(n,n))
image(graph)

The 'graph' object can be supplied in Besag's like models as
   f(..., graph=graph)

best,
Elias

